import json,html,sys
from pathlib import Path
r=json.load(open('dev/two-point-audit-results.json'));c=json.load(open('dev/two-point-controls.json'))
pct=lambda x:'—' if x is None else f'{x*100:.2f}%'
num=lambda x:'—' if x is None else f'{x:.3f}'
pp=lambda x:'—' if x is None else f'{x*100:+.3f} pp'
e=lambda x:html.escape(str(x))
out=[]
def p(s):out.append('<p>'+s+'</p>')
def h(s):out.append('<h2>'+e(s)+'</h2>')
def table(cols,rows):out.append('<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+e(x)+'</th>' for x in cols)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+e(x)+'</td>' for x in row)+'</tr>' for row in rows)+'</tbody></table></div>')
p('<strong>Only the verified no-sag-bonus correction is adopted. All two-point and second-chance work below is diagnostic.</strong> October 7, 2026.')
h('Scope, reproducibility and verification')
p('Fresh 30-team default 2026 male league, 15 rostered players/team, fixture seed 61005. 150 independent games, ten games/team, game seeds 100000–100149. Circle schedule: first ten rounds, venue alternating by round. Preseason league state reset before each game. This is a newly specified current-build fixture, not an exact replay of the earlier reference matchup list and not the user’s saved season. Its measured 123.84 PPG must not be interpreted as drift from the prior 123.67 result.')
p('All 150 instrumented games matched the uninstrumented no-sag engine in full game data AND full league state. Each passed FGA/FGM/3PA/3PM, rebound and score reconciliation. All 2,789 primary rim evaluations passed additive-modifier reconciliation. The final paired run took '+num(r['runtimeSeconds'])+' seconds. A repeat verification reproduced the same aggregate results; this remains 150 unique games, not 300 independent samples.')
p('Normal/headless seeded full-state parity passed; 40-game box-score/play-by-play checks passed. Simulation-rules tests passed after fixing their pre-existing missing await on sim(1). No production simulation behavior was changed by that test repair. Source observers exist only in the development runner and are never loaded by the application. Browser visual QA is unavailable in this environment; this change has no UI alterations.')
table(['Metric','New no-sag diagnostic'],[(k,pct(v) if k in ['FG','twoP','threeP'] else num(v))for k,v in r['league'].items()])
h('Offensive rebound → next action')
b=r['rebounds'];table(['Measure','Result'],[['OREB/team/game',num(b['perTeamGame'])],['OREB%',pct(b['rate'])],['Total OREB',b['total']],['Immediate putbacks',b['routes']['putback']],['Putback attempts/OREB',num(b['putbacksPerOreb'])],['Putbacks/team/game',num(b['putbacksPerTeamGame'])],['Putback share of all FGA',pct(r['paths']['putback']['share'])],['Putback FG%',pct(r['paths']['putback']['FG'])]])
table(['Mutually exclusive immediate route','Count','% of all OREB'],[[k,v,pct(v/b['total'])]for k,v in b['routes'].items()]+[['Direct turnover',0,'0%'],['Direct foul',0,'0%'],['Direct no-shot end',0,'0%'],['Other',0,'0%']])
p('All rebounds after an ordinary primary miss immediately choose a putback or kick-out. The putback branch uses the rebounder’s putback tendency (including archetype scaling). Offensive boards handled by finishRebound—after secondary misses or final missed free throws—re-enter the full possession engine instead. There is no third “reset first” option on the ordinary-miss route. This guarantees immediate shots on 86.30% of OREB; 71.11% are putbacks. That is a strong structural preference, but frequency alone does not establish that the basketball result is unrealistic.')
table(['First outcome after recursive reset','Count','% of recursive OREB','% of all OREB'],[[k,b['recursiveFirstEvents'].get(k,0),pct(b['recursiveFirstEvents'].get(k,0)/b['routes']['recursive']),pct(b['recursiveFirstEvents'].get(k,0)/b['total'])]for k in ['shot','turnover','foul','no shot','other']])
p('The recursive categories use the first shot evaluation/event: a missed shooting-foul evaluation without FGA is classified as foul; a made and-one remains a shot. These categories are nested under recursive, not added to the immediate-route table. OREB% = offensive boards / (offensive + defensive boards) across all tracked rebounds, including live missed-free-throw rebounds.')
h('Putback types and defensive selection')
table(['Type','Attempts','Share of putbacks','Finishing rating','Effective defender rim','Make probability','Observed FG%','Block rate'],[[k,v['attempts'],pct(v['attempts']/r['paths']['putback']['attempts']),num(v['rating']),num(v['rim']),pct(v['final']),pct(v['FG']),pct(v['blockRate'])]for k,v in r['putbacks'].items()])
p('lay = layup, dnk = dunk. No other immediate putback type exists. The defender is d from the preceding primary shot, after any primary ISO/PNR matchup reassignment. It is not reselected for the rebounder, nearest to the rebounder, or automatically the strongest rim protector. Putbacks use y("rim"), an effective rating closure whose fatigue progress was established for the primary matchup. A changed rebounder does not change that defender or stamina reference.')
p('After the board, rim defense still enters make probability at −0.002 per rating point. Rebounding, height, strength, vertical and positioning do not directly enter the layup putback make or block calculation. Their earlier rebound-selection effects still exist; dnk/jmp/reb/oiq plus standing-dunk tendency influence whether the putback is a dunk. Build/morale/rest wrappers have already adjusted raw attributes before the game, but putback finishing bypasses the additional per-possession effectiveAttribute calculation.')
h('Primary rim/layup variants — excludes all second-chance attempts')
rv=r['rimVariants'];table(['Variant','FGA','Share of primary rim FGA','Base + physical','Context','Final make-roll P','FG%','Contest rate','Block rate','Shooting foul/evaluation'],[[k,v['attempts'],pct(v['attempts']/r['primaryRim']['attempts']),pct(v['base']),pct(v['context']),pct(v['final']),pct(v['FG']),pct(v['contest']),pct(v['blockRate']),pct(v['foulRate'])]for k,v in rv.items()]+[['Standing layup',0,'0%','—','—','—','—','—','—','—']])
p('There is no separate standing-layup variant in the current primary resolver. “Running Layup” is selected when the transition flag is true; that flag can also be sampled from coach tempo, so it does not always mean an actual fast break after a turnover. Probability/contest/block columns use recorded FGA. Foul rate uses all evaluations, including foul misses excluded from FGA. Final probability is conditional on the make-roll branch, not inclusive of block risk.')
h('Primary rim contest and help')
cols=['Group','FGA','Finishing rating','Effective rim defense','Final probability','FG%','Block rate']
table(cols,[[k,v['attempts'],num(v['rating']),num(v['rim']),pct(v['final']),pct(v['FG']),pct(v['blockRate'])]for k,v in r['rimContest'].items()])
table(cols,[[k,v['attempts'],num(v['rating']),num(v['rim']),pct(v['final']),pct(v['FG']),pct(v['blockRate'])]for k,v in r['rimHelp'].items()])
p('Help arrival is explicitly sampled in PNR roll coverage; the audit observes that actual branch. Outside it there is no universal “help arrived” flag. There is no standalone “rim protector involved” boolean: the selected defender’s rim rating and physical attributes are used. Position is available but is not equivalent to rim-protector involvement; no synthetic designation was invented.')
h('Base versus ratings, physical matchup and context')
rp=r['rimEvaluationPipeline'];table(['Stage','All primary rim evaluations'],[['Fixed inside base','62.500%'],['After rating differential / physical contest scaling',pct(rp['ratingBase'])],['After physical drive/post/recovery',pct(rp['base'])],['After additive context',pct(rp['context'])],['Positive context',pp(rp['positive'])],['Negative context',pp(rp['negative'])],['Net context',pp(rp['net'])]])
p('The inside base is the largest starting component by construction, not proof that it is incorrectly calibrated. Rating/contest scaling adds about 1.46 pp and physical drive advantage another 0.515 pp. Additive context then adds 4.481 pp. Running-layup and PNR effects are the largest positive context contributors; a blanket base change would also hit dunks, floaters and post hooks.')
h('Every additive rim modifier')
table(['Modifier','Nonzero applications / 2,789','Mean when nonzero','Contribution across all primary rim evaluations'],[[k,v['applied'],pp(v['meanApplied']),pp(v['contribution'])]for k,v in r['rimModifiers'].items()])
p('These contributions average over primary rim evaluations, not all league shots. ShotVariant is the final shot.adjustment term; the following breakdown identifies its actual layup variants. Physical terms are already included before this additive context table and must not be double-counted.')
table(['Physical term','Applications','Mean when applied','Contribution'],[[k,v['applied'],pp(v['meanApplied']),pp(v['contribution'])]for k,v in r['rimPhysicalModifiers'].items()])
table(['Variant adjustment','Evaluations','Mean adjustment','Contribution across all primary rim evaluations'],[[k,v['n'],pp(v['mean']),pp(v['contribution'])]for k,v in r['rimVariantAdjustment'].items()])
table(['Stack','Evaluations','Base','Context','Net context'],[[k,v['n'],pct(v['base']),pct(v['context']),pp(v['net'])]for k,v in r['rimStacks'].items()])
p('Potential overlap: running layups receive +5.5 pp and half the normal layup block multiplier; an uncontested state separately adds +1.5 pp. PNR choice and screen boost can stack on top. The 158 running + PNR + screen-boost + uncontested evaluations average +12.938 pp net context. This is evidence of correlated reward stacking, not proof that every overlapping effect is unintended.')
h('Controlled equal-rating probabilities')
p(e(c['scope']))
scenarios=['neutral','contested','uncontested','driving','cutting','running','dunk','floater','postHook']
table(['Shot / state']+[str(n)+' vs '+str(n)for n in [60,70,75,80,90]],[[s]+[pct(next(x['probability']for x in c['equal']if x['scenario']==s and x['rating']==n))for n in [60,70,75,80,90]]for s in scenarios])
p('These are non-foul make-roll probabilities before the separate block roll. Neutral, uncontested and ordinary driving are identical under these specified neutral conditions: the engine has only contested/uncontested states, not a third neutral contest category. Physical size is matched, team-IQ baseline is 70, coaches equal with fit 60, home court off, no lineup advantages or sag. Dunks use standing-dunk strength adjustment; other raw attributes equal the shown rating. Fixed player/defender rating differences cancel at every equal-rating pair.')
h('Controlled 75-rated finishing versus rim defense')
table(['Rim defense','Uncontested normal layup','Contested normal layup','Layup putback','Dunk putback'],[[v['defense']]+[pct(v[k]['probability'])for k in ['uncontested','contested','layupPutback','dunkPutback']]for v in c['putbacks']])
table(['Rim defense','Normal uncontested incl. blocks','Normal contested incl. blocks','Layup putback incl. blocks','Dunk putback incl. blocks'],[[v['defense']]+[pct(v[k]['expectedNonFoulFG'])for k in ['uncontested','contested','layupPutback','dunkPutback']]for v in c['putbacks']])
p('Only rim defense varies; all other attributes are 75 and block tendency is 50%. Primary layup block risk is 4.75%; putback layup 0%; putback dunk 4%. All four make-probability paths decline by 6 pp from 60 to 90 rim defense. Putbacks are therefore not insensitive to rim defense in the base equation. Their missing/additional gates are the inconsistency.')
h('Dunks: misses and rating differentiation')
d=r['dunkMisses'];p(f'All dunk paths: {pct(r["categories"]["dunk"]["FG"])} on {r["categories"]["dunk"]["attempts"]:,} FGA. Of {d["total"]:,} misses, {d["blocked"]:,} ({pct(d["blocked"]/d["total"])}) were blocks and {d["makeRoll"]:,} ({pct(d["makeRoll"]/d["total"])}) failed make rolls. Blocks matter, but most misses come from conversion probability. Dunks share the .625 inside base; they are not modeled as near-automatic finishes.')
table(['Dunk-rating band','FGA','Avg effective finishing','Avg defender rim','Final probability','FG%','Block rate'],[[k,v['attempts'],num(v['rating']),num(v['rim']),pct(v['final']),pct(v['FG']),pct(v['blockRate'])]for k,v in sorted(r['dunkBands'].items())])
p('Observed rating-band accuracy is not monotonic: this sample does NOT establish that elite dunkers meaningfully outperform poor dunkers in ordinary matchups. Different defense, path and shot mixes confound the groups; under-60 has only 225 attempts. The controlled rating formula remains monotonic, shown below.')
table(['Dunk rating only varies','Make probability','Including block risk'],[[v['dunkRating'],pct(v['probability']),pct(v['expectedNonFoulFG'])]for v in c['dunkSensitivity']])
p('Primary dunk effective finishing loses '+num(-r['primaryCategories']['dunk']['fatigueOnlyDelta'])+' rating points on average from in-game fatigue alone (about '+num(-r['primaryCategories']['dunk']['fatigueOnlyDelta']*.2)+' pp in its raw rating term, before clamps). This is a within-shot arithmetic observation, not an alternate simulation. Defense, physical context and shot selection still affect final outcomes; fatigue alone does not explain the roughly 39% miss rate.')
h('Floaters, midrange and post')
table(['Category, all paths','FGA','Base + physical','Context','Final','FG%','Net context'],[[k,r['categories'][k]['attempts'],pct(r['categories'][k]['base']),pct(r['categories'][k]['context']),pct(r['categories'][k]['final']),pct(r['categories'][k]['FG']),pp(r['categories'][k]['contextDelta'])]for k in ['floater','midrange','post']])
p('Floaters inherit .625, then explicit floater −.045/−.055 and touch −.025 adjustments. At equal ratings, a neutral uncontested floater is still 57% before blocks. Observed floater context is negative (about −6.20 pp); positive context stacking is not the main explanation for its remaining efficiency. The high starting inside base is the stronger explanation. Its block multiplier is .4. Post mixes inside hooks with midrange fades/turnarounds, so its average base is between .625 and .435. No separate structural midrange/post issue was established by this lighter audit.')
h('Primary versus immediate putback resolver')
table(['Element','Primary rim','Immediate putback','Classification'],[
 ['Shooter attributes','effectiveAttribute with adaptation, IQ/personality, morale/chemistry, in-game fatigue','Match-local raw lay/dnk; earlier outer wrappers still applied','LIKELY BUG: asymmetric effective-rating treatment'],
 ['Fatigue','Current shooter stamina and starter workload','No rebounder-specific in-game fatigue','LIKELY BUG'],
 ['Defender selection','Position/archetype matchup or PNR/ISO selected defender','Previous shot defender reused','QUESTIONABLE'],
 ['Defender attributes','Effective attributes for primary matchup','Same y(rim) closure, tied to primary matchup progress','QUESTIONABLE'],
 ['Physical matchup','Height contest scale; weight/post and drive/recovery effects','No new rebounder/defender physical matchup','QUESTIONABLE'],
 ['Contest','Contested −.015; uncontested +.015 for inside; shot multiplier','No contest state or adjustment','QUESTIONABLE'],
 ['Help defense','PNR roll can choose arriving helper','No new help selection','QUESTIONABLE'],
 ['Block attempt','Block tendency × rating/height/jump/strength formula × variant','Layup: impossible. Dunk: block tendency × .08, no block ability term','LIKELY BUG for un-blockable layups; QUESTIONABLE simplified dunk rule'],
 ['Shooting foul','Draw-foul and defender IQ/discipline/foul rate, then FT sequence','No shooting-foul gate','QUESTIONABLE; omission can also suppress points'],
 ['Turnover opportunity','Full decision/handling/pass gates','None before immediate putback','INTENTIONAL direct finish simplification; no rebalance inferred'],
 ['Context modifiers','PNR/ISO/variant/IQ/coaches/lineup etc.','None of primary additive context','INTENTIONAL action-specific simplification; fatigue omission is separate'],
 ['Sliders','shootingRate then shot-specific accuracy','Same shootingRate and lay/dunk accuracy','INTENTIONAL / consistent'],
 ['Home court','Same homeCourtProbability','Same homeCourtProbability','INTENTIONAL / consistent'],
 ['Clamps','Base [.02,.98]; non-foul [.02,.88], foul [.05,.65], sliders/home [0,1]','Base [.02,.98], sliders/home [0,1]; no primary .88 cap','QUESTIONABLE'],
 ['Miss handling','Rebound selection; optional immediate second chance','finishRebound then full recursive action on OREB','INTENTIONAL alternating routes; guarantees immediate shot after ordinary-miss OREB'],
])
p('INTENTIONAL marks an action-specific distinction consistent with the code’s direct-finish design, not confirmation of the original author’s rationale. QUESTIONABLE means a plausible simplification needing a design decision. LIKELY BUG marks a concrete inconsistent capability/attribute path; none are fixed in this task.')
h('Second-chance scoring value')
s=r['secondChance'];table(['Measure','Result'],[['Points after OREB, total',s['points']],['Second-chance points/team/game',num(s['perTeamGame'])],['Points/OREB',num(s['pointsPerOreb'])],['Points/100 OREB',num(s['pointsPer100Oreb'])],['Immediate putback points/team/game',num(s['immediatePutbackPointsPerTeamGame'])],['Possessions with OREB',s['withOrebPossessions']],['Total PPP, possession with OREB',num(s['withOrebPPP'])],['PPP without OREB',num(s['withoutOrebPPP'])],['No-OREB, no-transition-flag PPP',num(s['halfCourtWithoutOrebPPP'])]])
p('Points are counted once after the first offensive rebound through that possession’s end, including subsequent free throws and further rebounds. Multiple rebounds do not duplicate scoring; the denominator still counts every OREB. The with-OREB PPP includes any points before the first rebound (for example, an and-one basket followed by a missed FT). Technical points for the opposing side are not credited as second-chance offense. Score-ledger reconciliation explicitly accounts for such points.')
p('Possessions with OREB score more in total, as expected from another opportunity. But 1.181 points per individual OREB is not demonstrably excessive against 1.184 PPP for possessions without OREB in this sample. The half-court proxy excludes possessions with any transition flag and is selected, not a randomized causal comparison. No external real-world benchmark was used; this audit does not establish a realistic target or justify changing rebound frequency.')
h('Conclusion and one next experiment')
p('<strong>Primary measured contributor:</strong> the .625 inside foundation plus favorable finishing/rating selection and correlated running/PNR/uncontested bonuses. Primary rim context adds 4.481 pp across evaluations, with running-layup variant and PNR choice the largest positive components. Floaters remain efficient despite negative context because they start from the same high inside base.')
p('<strong>Secondary contributor:</strong> ordinary-miss offensive rebounds guarantee immediate putback/kick-out shots; layup putbacks bypass blocks and rebounder fatigue. These paths are structurally inconsistent, but their total causal contribution to scoring inflation has not yet been isolated.')
p('<strong>Recommended next experiment — ONE change only:</strong> apply the existing primary layup block-check formula to immediate layup putbacks, using the rebounder and the currently selected defender. Keep defender selection, raw make probability, fatigue, putback frequency, rebound rates, fouls, pace, ratings, dunk putbacks and every other modifier unchanged for that experiment. This isolates the concrete zero-block path before attempting a wider resolver refactor. <strong>Not implemented.</strong>')
p('Source locations: dist/attributes.js — possessionCore, finishRebound, effectiveAttribute; dist/statistical-balance.js — basketballShotProbability, selectBasketballRebound; dist/tendencies.js — layupOptions, contextualLayup, dunkFinish, putbackDunkChance, jumperFinish; dist/pick-and-roll.js — playPickAndRoll; dist/physical-build.js — physicalMatchup; dist/simulation-rules.js — shotMakeProbability.')
out.append('<details><summary>Machine-readable measured results</summary><pre>'+e(json.dumps({'audit':r,'controls':c},indent=2))+'</pre></details>')
page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Hoops Dynasty — Two-Point and Second-Chance Audit</title><style>body{font:16px/1.6 system-ui;background:#f4f6f8;color:#172939;margin:0}main{max-width:1280px;margin:auto;padding:30px}h1{line-height:1.2}h2{margin-top:36px;border-bottom:2px solid #b99650}table{border-collapse:collapse;background:white;width:100%;font-size:14px}th,td{border:1px solid #d5dfe5;padding:9px;text-align:left}th{background:#193449;color:white}.scroll{overflow:auto}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:12px}@media(max-width:600px){main{padding:16px}}</style><main><h1>Hoops Dynasty<br>Two-Point &amp; Second-Chance Scoring Audit</h1>'''+''.join(out)+'</main></html>'
Path(sys.argv[1]).write_text(page)
